---
source: crates/zeff-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "out(&zeff(dir.path(), &[\"help\", \"print\"]))"
---
print — Print values                                                         core · tier 0 · since 0.1.0 · 1.0 · exact

USAGE
    print(x, ...)

DESCRIPTION
    Prints each value through the display interface that `core` declares and every type implements, so a
    frame, a table, a number or a text prints the way it prints when a statement that is not a `let` stands
    on its own: an Int in full, a Float to six significant digits, text and Bool as they are, `NA` as
    written, a list one item per line, a frame as its header and first ten rows, a table as its title and
    rows. Several values print one after another, each on its own lines.

    `print` returns nothing: it is a statement, and its result cannot be bound or passed on (Z0206).

ARGUMENTS
    x           Any. The value to print; any type.
    ...         Any. Further values, each printed after the one before.

VALUE
    Nothing.

WARNINGS AND NOTES
    Z0206   the result of print is bound or passed; it has none

ACCURACY
    Exact.

SEE ALSO
    describe, summary

EXAMPLES
    > print(42)
    42
    > print("hello", 0.1)
    hello
    0.1
    > print(true, NA, 0.1, 1e15, [1, 2.5])
    true
    NA
    0.1
    1e+15
    1
    2.5
    > let d = frame(x = [1, 2], y = ["a", "b"])
    > print(d.n_rows(), d)
    2
    d · 2 rows × 2 variables

          x   y
      1   1   a
      2   2   b
